<addressbook><name>KARASAWA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASAKA, YOSHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUWANETSUKOGYO CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KARASAWA HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYASAKA YOSHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KARASAWA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASAKA, YOSHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A ball for ball-point pen and a ball-point pen using the ball excellent in wear resistance and lubricity and capable of being manufactured easily, wherein a stainless steel is used as a material and a nitrosulphurized layer is formed on the surface of the material to constitute the ball (2) for ball-point pen, or an aluminum chrome molybdenum steel is used as a material and the nitrosulphurized layer is formed on the surface of the material to constitute the ball (2) for ball-point pen, whereby a ball-point pen using the ball provides an excellent sharpness in writing.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une bille pour stylo à bille et un stylo à bille pourvu de cette bille, laquelle présente une excellente résistance à l'usure, une bonne caractéristique de glissement et peut être fabriquée facilement. Un acier inoxydable est utilisé comme matière sur la surface de laquelle est formée une couche nitrosulfurisée de manière à constituer la bille (2) pour stylo à bille. Un acier au chrome, au molybdène et à l'aluminium peut également être utilisé comme matière sur la surface de laquelle est formée une couche nitrosulfurisée de manière à constituer la bille (2) pour stylo à bille. Un stylo à bille muni d'une telle bille permet d'écrire de manière très nette.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>